OpenStax textbook content
=========================

Textbook content produced by OpenStax (Rice University) is licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The books below are the ones configured in config/subjects.yaml. Each subject's
attribution line from that file is returned with every answer from
/api/v1/ask and /api/v1/ask/stream and is shown in the chat UI.

Seeded by default (US History and Economics)

  * US History, OpenStax
    Book page:  https://openstax.org/details/books/us-history
    Fetched from the community mirror https://github.com/philschatz/us-history-book

  * Principles of Economics, OpenStax (configured book title: "Economics")
    Book page:  https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-economics-3e
    Fetched from the community mirror https://github.com/philschatz/economics-book

Configured but not seeded by default

  * Biology 2e, OpenStax
    Book page:  https://openstax.org/details/books/biology-2e
    Fetched from the community mirror https://github.com/philschatz/biology-book

  * Concepts of Biology, OpenStax
    Fetched from the community mirror https://github.com/philschatz/biology-concepts-book

  * World History, Volume 1 and Volume 2, OpenStax
    Attribution link: https://openstax.org/subjects/humanities
    Fetched from https://openstax.org/books/world-history-volume-1 and
    https://openstax.org/books/world-history-volume-2

OpenStax material included in this repository

  * data/raw/us_history/ holds US History modules in Markdown, as published by
    the mirror listed above.
  * data/processed/ holds sections normalized to JSON Lines and knowledge
    graphs extracted from US History and Economics.

Changes made to the material: the text was converted to Markdown and JSON,
split into sections and retrieval chunks, embedded for vector search, and used
to extract concepts and the relationships between them. Generated answers and
quiz questions quote or paraphrase retrieved passages.

Access the original books for free at https://openstax.org/.


